2ec-bda0-b8559134189b", "type": "concept", "title": "Phrase boundary"}], "description": "True modulation requires evidence of a new key area, not just accidentals."}, {"id": "2e02c58d-3696-4800-b426-3efa04ee66bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Key-area mapping", "children": [{"id": "51bb85b0-f324-4fec-aeac-beab03cd206b", "type": "concept", "title": "Home key"}, {"id": "6b71b9ab-a87c-470e-a3d7-f39c49bf7acb", "type": "concept", "title": "Closely related keys"}, {"id": "5fc534d6-36d8-49e2-b526-b99af160e1f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Dominant key"}, {"id": "b3ee35e7-8c52-48bf-a723-e3a7a4765363", "type": "concept", "title": "Relative major/minor"}], "description": "Students track where music travels and how it returns."}]}, {"id": "99886c25-8a92-4a05-8dd5-b36a9947b4a1", "type": "topic", "title": "Error Detection and Diagnostic Listening", "description": "Strengthens the ability to compare score and sound, identify mistakes, and explain corrections precisely.", "children": [{"id": "d34f2944-ad74-45e7-98a5-f6772253195f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Score-to-sound comparison", "children": [{"id": "a6ed1636-f74b-4819-83ca-7def77f89053", "type": "concept", "title": "Pitch errors"}, {"id": "123b5e8f-ee07-4e03-8236-46abb247259d", "type": "concept", "title": "Rhythm errors"}, {"id": "c7a26926-c190-433d-a4df-a83eb466d613", "type": "concept", "title": "Wrong chord quality"}, {"id": "0015a0f3-4aa6-4480-9341-38e070d67558", "type": "concept", "title": "Missing accidentals"}], "description": "Students learn to hear discrepancies between written notation and performance."}, {"id": "9ea22454-3b3a-47f1-98ea-2f5e537ab08e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diagnostic language", "children": [{"id": "f06c92df-c04f-44cf-8570-8ad921665646", "type": "concept", "title": "Too high/low"}, {"id": "73990efc-fd10-4b81-8800-2cf40f67c1c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Early/late"}, {"id": "a3094356-13e6-470e-a60a-8f9497ae6db6", "type": "concept", "title": "Wrong function"}, {"id": "4cd0af1a-ee59-4bb7-8253-b1c2dcf7fcc2", "type": "concept", "title": "Incorrect resolution"}], "description": "Useful error detection names both the problem and the likely correction."}, {"id": "e9b25109-7555-4158-96ab-3bc2ac476e6d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ensemble correction", "children": [{"id": "53999bda-f06b-4d1d-95a2-8fd4d599521b", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer feedback"}, {"id": "ae747917-b25f-44ad-abb3-896fb39d50e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Conductor cues"}, {"id": "53b6efb5-63db-4012-950e-d5c8001316ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Section listening"}, {"id": "ac56d214-547b-4f14-ad2d-2db9ed6d52d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-correction"}], "description": "Students practice listening in ways that support rehearsal, not just individual testing."}]}, {"id": "8e7d8226-9747-4ef2-a237-3268ce920dc3", "type": "topic", "title": "Improvised Melodies and Aural Creativity", "description": "Uses improvisation to prove functional hearing, rhythmic control, phrase awareness, and stylistic fluency.", "children": [{"id": "7d17fe96-966a-4947-a01e-eb766d2ac0f8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Functional improvisation", "children": [{"id": "3fdef337-1fdf-40ee-bb0d-517495ff5f34", "type": "concept", "title": "Tonic-dominant phrases"}, {"id": "36c4c9b9-3b1f-4490-89dc-2e423d744c1c", "type": "concept", "title": "Question-answer"}, {"id": "0cfb1957-94b6-4438-9c11-e2795e12674d", "type": "concept", "title": "Cadence targeting"}, {"id": "be089e3e-101e-4bf2-ba8d-26df02f8902f", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequence"}], "description": "Improvisation reveals whether students can use what they hear in real time."}, {"id": "4145d57e-afee-4d9b-95bd-392308ecd3e5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rhythmic invention", "children": [{"id": "b697a64b-fe4e-491c-a387-f8d7a61289d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Motivic rhythm"}, {"id": "0c46f5f5-4d64-4b39-9cff-d687109ec26d", "type": "concept", "title": "Syncopation"}, {"id": "41d1f92e-1737-4191-9ee1-1f27d0d9699b", "type": "concept", "title": "Variation"}, {"id": "8cc920e4-7928-405f-9c53-bfe25c29d99b", "type": "concept", "title": "Call-and-response"}], "description": "Students apply rhythmic vocabulary creatively while maintaining pulse and meter."}, {"id": "63c21bfe-9ce2-45c4-bf9a-f5c42292a707", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Style and constraint", "children": [{"id": "fb1fb348-b66e-4bd6-9172-3f6762b7b929", "type": "concept", "title": "Given scale degrees"}, {"id": "1441a9c7-9f16-4f7c-8f59-273c17b3d7eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Given rhythm"}, {"id": "40b8ded1-a624-45d9-ae49-21a89d30328c", "type": "concept", "title": "Given harmony"}, {"id": "b8581add-ec2a-4a3a-873f-5feade778a6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Phrase length"}], "description": "Limited prompts help students improvise with purpose rather than wandering."}]}, {"id": "ef8592bc-f702-4c84-9fa2-764986c5e79a", "type": "topic", "title": "Conducting While Singing and Embodied Coordination", "description": "Integrates singing, conducting, pulse, breath, and meter so students can coordinate multiple musicianship tasks.", "children": [{"id": "82d0f097-65ee-4993-8d06-e55d965c4c99", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conducting patterns", "children": [{"id": "375d1562-f8ed-4feb-a745-a73a2920b4b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Two, three, and four patterns"}, {"id": "95b1980a-8ddb-4b81-ae43-f5087063a2ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Compound patterns"}, {"id": "d7974324-b927-4d13-a2bf-3241d1c27557", "type": "concept", "title": "Preparatory gesture"}, {"id": "4cba241b-b47a-4598-85d3-db789164749b", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutoff"}], "description": "Conducting while singing strengthens meter, breath, and ensemble leadership."}, {"id": "e8912aef-6397-46ac-9545-ece18b80a75f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multitask coordination", "children": [{"id": "768e40c4-fa06-49b3-b093-7451e15e677d", "type": "concept", "title": "Sing and conduct"}, {"id": "848fb24d-4cc3-48a4-ba9f-77106d1967a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Speak rhythm and conduct"}, {"id": "c61b8405-f9d1-4